    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d440">

                <pb facs="0598" n="454" xml:id="pg454"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.11/972</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The American Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">MacMurray</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the British Minister in China</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lampson</hi>)<anchor n="61"
                        xml:id="d440-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peking</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1929-04-30">April 30, 1929</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir and Dear Colleague</hi>: I have the honor to
                    acknowledge the receipt of your communication of April 26th informing me that,
                    in view of the recent disturbances at Changteh and reports that foreign life was
                    in danger, a British Naval landing party from H.M.S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Widgeon</hi> proceeded there on April 18th in an armed motor-tug
                    accompanied by Mr. Harding, His Majesty’s Consul at Changsha, who later reported
                    to you that the party returned to Changsha on April 22nd bringing with them a
                    number of refugees, including two American citizens, Mr. Tootell and Miss
                    Jacobson, but that an American family named Wager declined to leave Changteh,
                    although the situation there was disquieting at the time.</p>
                <p>Please accept my warmest thanks for the very real service rendered by this
                    British party to the American citizens concerned. I shall be grateful if you
                    will express to Mr. Harding and to the British Naval authorities my appreciation
                    of their services.</p>
                <p>I avail myself [etc.]</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">J. V. A.
                    MacMurray</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d440-f1" n="61" type="source" xml:id="d440-f1-content">
